n who broke  down in tears  i myself lost my father we have only  just reached the first year anniversary  of his death from covid in fact today  would have been him and my mother's 52nd  wedding anniversary so there's a lot of  pain associated with what's going on and  you know these  revelations that we are hearing almost  on a weekly basis  yeah we had a break for christmas um a  new year but they're back and who knows  how much more will come but each time  we learn something new  our pain and our wounds that we are  trying to get through and our grieving  process is impacted  and we're bracing ourselves for more  so you're saying that that the news that  you're hearing is actually making your  grief worse  absolutely we're still trying to heal  the grieving process for the families  that have lost loved ones to covert  uh has been challenging because there  are so many unknown entities there are  so many questions and we need answers  and that's why an inquiry an independent  inquiry into the way that the government  managed covert in this country is so  critical and so crucial thank goodness  we now finally have a chair appointed  and the process will begin soon i hope  but  this drip feed of revelations of what  we're learning is painful but crucially  important it kind of is like the warm up  to the to the main act i think because i  think  yes what we're learning now is terrible  but what more is to come and only when  this is done and dealt with and out  there and there has been proper  accountability will we then finally be  able to heal it won't happen until then  what were the restrictions like around  the time that your dad died and and how  did they affect  how much time you were able to to be  with him  so let's let's go back to may when when  this alleged party took place and the  invitations were sent out and  you know this wasn't a a knee-jerk let's  get together  this was a pre-meditated arranged  gathering with invitations of up to 100  sent out at the same time as  the rest of us were being told um by  politicians advised by their scientific  advisors that only we could only meet  one person at a time so at the time of  the party the alleged party  restrictions were pretty fierce and  let's go back to remind ourselves of the  environment that we were living in we  were in the pre-k we were in the  pre-vaccine days  medics and scientists not just in the uk  but around the globe we're still trying  to work out how this virus is really  impacting us we were still trying to  work out within hospitals what the  correct ppe measures were we were having  our pp i i at that time was working  emergency medicine within a e moving  into intensive care we were at that  point still trying to work out the safe  ways of working within hospitals staff  members my colleagues were living in  tents outside their own homes for fear  of passing on infection my questions as  a doctor  and as a member of the public anna's  someone who has lost a loved one to  covert and knows the reality of how  easily the disease was being transmitted  last year  and still continues to be  that but with now with the caveat of  safety measures in place the vaccine and  face masks at that point we didn't have  that all so strictly in place so i want  to know how many infections did these  gatherings arranged by uh 10 downing  street and by  the various offices within government  how many how much more infection spread  did that lead to and my other question  is this  uh  this is a finite group of people  people are in the know whenever you have  a community or a group of people people  tend to know what's going on how many  people who are speaking to us on a daily  basis from their podiums from number 10  knew about these things so once they on  the one hand were telling us scientific  evidence says that we are now going down  to only one you can only meet one person  at the time uh to ensure correct safety  measures with uh uh  with kerbin covered spread how many of  them knew about these gatherings how  many had that email sitting in their  inbox during the day when they came to  speak to us in the evening these are all  questions that need answering and the  only people that will be able to  investigate this properly are the police  and in terms of your dad you you know  you're saying that you were renee at  that time but many of your siblings are  also doctors as well aren't they how did  that affect your ability to be with your  dad  during that period of time my brother  actually caught covid from working  within hospitals so in april last year  myself and my brother were holed up in a  flat um  being very ill and and and isolating  when we were covered and bearing mine he  caught it from hospital from work  um in may when we emerged and we were  going out and about  we were then terrified about going  anywhere near my father um five of us  are doctors we didn't go we we reduced  our contact with our father who was left  alone for the majority of time during  that year we were  torn between  looking after our patients on the front  line and doing now atmos to what we  signed up for which is essentially  caring for others um to then neglecting  our own father it was a really  challenging year really really  challenging but we did what we had to do  ultimately he did catch covert at the  end but what is really painful  is that we spent so much time away from  him  because those were the rules and we knew  that those were the correct rules  because uh any form of contact could  have  given him uh  the virus  and so many other people were sticking  to the walls because not only were they  worried about themselves they were  worried about others  i feel that the thursday night clapping  that was being that was taking place on  this on the steps of number 10 it was  just a mockery there was so  this whole episode smacks  of disrespect to those of us that were  working on the front line a lack of  respect and understanding for those of  us that lost loved ones and i fear that  there is more to come  dr dr salia assange we're going to have  to leave it there uh really good to talk  to you thank you for talking to us about  your experience and the loss of your dad  as well  you're watching sky news today coming up  next with sarah jane me boris johnson  under fire over the revelations about a  downing street party held during the  height of lockdown  [Music]  you
 

